problem_statement:
Flex containers not positioned correctly when their margin-left/right is set to `auto`
In the following example, a flex container (the `.inner` div) has its `margin-left` and `margin-right` properties set to `auto`, which should cause it to be centered in its parent div. Instead, it is positioned at the left edge of the `.outer` div.
WeasyPrint does this correctly when the inner div gets changed to `display: block`.

(This may or may not be related to https://github.com/Kozea/WeasyPrint/issues/1171, although that issues talks about nested flex containers, whereas in my case the outer container is a normal block element.)

```html
<style>
  .outer {
    background: red;
  }
  
  .inner {
    margin: auto;
    display: flex;
    width: 10rem;
    height: 10rem;
    background: black;
  }
</style>

<div class="outer">
  <div class="inner"></div>
</div>
```

![image](https://github.com/Kozea/WeasyPrint/assets/816758/12a0fb16-6f39-484b-8369-61ec225374ae)

